The trigger would fire, call the `on_upkeep` function, check if the active player is the controller, find they're not, and return immediately without setting any action state. The trigger resolves silently with no visible effect. The oracle text says the ability should only trigger during the controller's upkeep, so technically the implementation is firing when it shouldn't, even though the end result is functionally identical. Given the strict audit rules, this is a technical inaccuracy I should flag, though it has zero gameplay impact. I'll note it and move on to check the rest of the card.

